    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. is a public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, trading under the ticker SERV and registered with the SEC under CIK 0001832483. Its website frames its work around the last-mile delivery problem, asking why a 2-pound burrito should be moved in a 2-ton car, and describes its robot as a low-emissions, self-driving delivery solution. The company says it is setting a standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, and that it protects customer data, its employees, and the public.\n\nThe site also presents the robot as a pop culture figure. It names the robot Saymo, which it says delivers burritos and appears as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\"\n\nThe corporate record adds the public listing, the ticker, the CIK, and the San Carlos headquarters. No lawsuits are listed against the company, and no products are listed under its name. Its legal exposure is recorded in California, with a count of 281.",
